A||||9||sqoach||Back from Cali!||||10||
Z||000000||sqoach||08-17-2001||02:04 AM||||Wow! What a trip! California is a beautiful state, for the most part! And it seems that just about all the cars are nice. No clunkers and junkers like around here. Guess that's because of the smog tests and stuff. Seemed like about 6 or 7 cars took up half the car population. BMW, Porsche, Civic, Miata, Grand Am, and Lexus. I swear everywhere I looked, I saw at least one of those.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> But it was cool. Saw 4 Ferrari's: a 308/328 and 3 360 Modena's(?) two silver, one blue. Saw a couple Vipers, 3 or 4 NSX's, a dozen MR2 Spyder's, S2000's, Prowler's. It was nice to see so many awesome cars.<BR>I also got to see quite a few Fiero's. Went by the Fieroshop, but nobody was there. Didn't really have time to stop by again. Met Bill (DXR_DAD) at the Niles car show. He's a cool guy. And his Fiero is nice! Black looks really good. And the stock rims were nice too! Very clean and shiny. We checked out some of the classics. Very nice show. Had some strange cars/things too. Lots of camaros and mustangs. Some nice hotrods, too.<BR>San Francisco was nice. Got to drive up and down the hilly streets. It was cool, and kinda scary at times. Very steep hills. It would be interesting to live there. Rode the trolly car. That was pretty neat. Went on a boat ride around Alcatraz(sp?) and under the Golden Gate bridge. Went to Hollywood on the walk of fame. Almost got to see Nicolas Cage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but it was really packed.<P>Anyway, since this post is so long, I should probably end it now. Just wanted to share. It was a blast! Wish I didn't have to leave. Maybe next year we'll go back...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||10
Z||000001||fierobaby||08-17-2001||02:24 AM||||sqoach,<P>glad you had a great time I went to Cali last summer and had an amazing time I saw the walk of fame right after the put in Samual L. Jacksons star... you could still see some of the sealer they leave on it to keep it nice. Hope you took some pics of the trip I did not get to see San Fransisco but would love to see some pics TTYL<P>Corinne<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-17-2001||02:41 AM||||Man......I missed another forum member!  I was just in the L.A. & San Fran area (got back last night).<P>I'm glad you had a good time.....my trip was all business, so I couldn't go sightseeing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||sloth85GT||08-17-2001||04:25 AM||||Hey sqoach, good to see you back. I didn't know you were gone, but once I stopped seeing posts I put two and two together. Now it's my turn for a little vacation. Going to Vancouver on Sunday for 7 days, then to Calgary for 2. It's gonna be a fun trip, great to get away from work. I just can't wait! Great to hear you had a fun time and got to see lots of sweet rides. <P>Vacations rule!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||08-17-2001||02:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>sqoach,<P>glad you had a great time I went to Cali last summer and had an amazing time I saw the walk of fame right after the put in Samual L. Jacksons star... you could still see some of the sealer they leave on it to keep it nice. Hope you took some pics of the trip I did not get to see San Fransisco but would love to see some pics TTYL<P>Corinne<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks. We went on the walk of fame too. It was right after Nicolas Cage "made his mark" on his star. It was neat. Didn't get to see the Hollywood sign. Couldn't find it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>We got to go to the Tonight Show on Tuesday. I wasn't real excited, but thought it would be cool. Turned out to be really cool. The set looks so small when you're in there. Jay seemed like a cool guy, too. Didn't get to meet him personally, though.<BR>My mom took tons of pictures. She took 100 pictures in less than 2 days up around San Francisco  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> We don't have a scanner, but I'll see what I can do.<BR>Sorry I didn't get to see you mrfiero. I didn't know you were taking a trip over there. I didn't have a lot of time to meet people, that's why I suggested meeting at the car show. Maybe some other time. We might go to Colorado for a few days near winter time.<BR>sloth, I posted a while back that I was leaving for vacation. Of course not everyone saw it. I'll let you know when I can get that spoiler to you, if you still want it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||08-17-2001||03:39 PM||||Glad you made it home!!!!! It was nice to meet you and your family. Next time your out this way we'll hang a little more??? So I can show you some of my Rods! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723603&p=18231081&Sequence=3&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=18365636&Sequence=2&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=18230214&Sequence=1&res=high"> <P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
